      <article class="legal-card">
        <section class="legal-section" id="payment-card-updates">
          <span class="legal-kicker">Payment Card Updates</span>
          <h2>Use the secure path for your booking channel.</h2>
          <p>If you booked directly with Seascape, payment-card updates should happen through the secure guest-portal link for your reservation. For your safety, do not send full card numbers by email, text, or voicemail.</p>
          <p>If you booked through Airbnb or Vrbo, make payment changes in your Airbnb or Vrbo account so the platform keeps the reservation record in sync.</p>
          <p>If you cannot find the right link, send us the name on the reservation and your stay dates. We can point you to the correct secure path.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section" id="booking-help">
          <span class="legal-kicker">Booking Help</span>
          <h3>Use the local team for reservation questions.</h3>
          <p>For booking questions, arrival timing, or a current-stay issue, contact Seascape directly. If it is urgent during your stay, use the emergency line included in your check-in instructions.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section" id="policy-details">
          <span class="legal-kicker">Policy Details</span>
          <h3>Your checkout page controls stay-specific terms.</h3>
          <p>Cancellation terms, deposits, and other reservation-specific details belong on the secure checkout or guest-portal page for your stay. This support page does not replace those details or add new payment promises.</p>
        </section>
      </article>

